\f1\fs22 Picture your grandmother. Now give her glossy white hair spun with gold. Let her have perfect teeth, and an unmottled complexion. Make her eyes clear and perceptive. Imagine she\'92s wearing a designer business suit in the season\'92s fashion; put the most sumptuous and cuddle-knitted shawl about her shoulders. She\'92s slender, and lithe, all the way down to her patent leather lawn-bowling shoes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Now transform her appearance a little\'97so, too, her carriage and deportment. Her spine is straight and her shoulders are square, and she reminds you a little of Candice Bergen, a little of Gloria Steinham, somewhat more of Jane Fonda, and a great deal of Daphne du Maurier.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Ah, there you almost have Eloise Shakti. All that remains is to assign her an expensively and ascetically clad entourage who remind you of dentists; or international assassins; or, perhaps both.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Now you have the right picture, then picture of Eloise visiting Sarah one morning.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah waited in the mansion\'92s parlour while Nancy showed Eloise and her international dentist-assassins in. After exchanging pleasantries, Eloise sat uprightly in a large-winged single-seater while Sarah comported herself from slouching on a lounge to something matching Eloise\'92s posture.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I understand you\'92re expecting,\'92 Eloise said, with a grandmotherly dose of warmth.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah answered with a pained and paralysed look of resigned terror.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Unplanned then,\'92 Eloise said, and Sarah half-expected her to append 
