<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>It took Sarah several seconds to process her bowels turning to ice and her skeleton to chalk. She stammered, \'91What\'92s a Gy\'92\'97\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sarah \'85 may I call you, Sarah? You won\'92t know this, but I\'92ve kept a keen interest in you for many years.\'92 Eloise took another sip of tea and dabbed her mouth with a napkin. \'91Many, many years. Quite a few more than anyone might give credit for.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>If Sarah was chilled before, Eloise\'92s words froze her to splinters.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The thing is, I think of you as family. For many reasons\'97some of which I suspect you appreciate very well indeed\'97you are close to my heart. So, I hope we can be on the same side of this, Sarah. Wouldn\'92t you like that too?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah animated her head enough to nod.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Excellent.\'92 If your grandmother was a snake that could smile, she\'92d smile exactly the way Eloise smiled. \'91The Gyges Disc, which is currently in your possession\'97\'92\
