<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Mike swallowed hard.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Shall I go on?\'92 Eloise asked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah felt something unfamiliar and diabolically rotten, like acid in her stomach and veins, concrete in her bones, splinters in her head. This must be how people feel when they\'92re beaten. \'91Ok, ok, I\'92ll get it.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise raised her eyebrow.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91It\'92s up stairs, in my room.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise nodded and Sarah ran.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>She returned with a handkerchief which she unfolded and presented to Eloise.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise took one look and waved it away in disgust. \'91What have you been doing? Blowing your nose on it?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah was paralysed. First Eloise killed for the disc, now she was shunning it?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Just put it on the table,\'92 Eloise instructed, then called, \'91Mr Stoat.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A large bald man, entered wearing an expensive suit so badly it looked cheap.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Johnny!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny couldn\'92t hold Sarah\'92s gaze. Instead, he picked up the hanky and examined the disc. \'91This\'92s it,\'92 he said as he folded the handkerchief around the disc.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Johnny?\'92 Sarah begged as if truly heart-broken. You work for her?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I\'92ve worked for one of her subsidiaries for years.\'92 Johnny pocketed the disc. \'91It\'92s not as if it\'92s a secret.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>It may as well have been a secret, for all the interest Sarah had for Johnny\'92s work life.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise, satisfied, rose. \'91Well, there ends the demonstration.\'92 On the way to the door, she pulled her entourage in behind, all but the one fallen, who she left for others to clean up. \'91Oh, one more thing,\'92 Eloise said, using the ol\'92 I-almost-forgot ploy. She gestured through the half-open door, summoning someone should come. A familiar face appeared alongside Eloise.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Tony!\'92 Sarah was so drained she could feel neither joy nor fury. But Tony still had much to answer for.\

